      "summary": ": 3 Sep 2026 Cardrona is open with firm, fast snow to start, broken cloud and patches of sunshine, while winds are expected to increase through the day. The latest mountain report records 3°C, winds around 40 km/h with gusts to 68 km/h, and a chance of precipitation later, possibly turning to snow during the afternoon. The grooming team has laid fresh cord overnight, although the resort warns that conditions may vary significantly off trail. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall’s Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar and Wells Pipe Platter are open. Soho Express is on hold and Willow’s Quad is closed for the day because of wind; McDougall’s was confirmed back open in the latest 1:20 pm update. The Platter is running for access to the Olympic Halfpipe until 10:45 am, and Masters Racing is taking place on Upper Gold Rush–Sluice Box. (Issued: 3 Sep, 1:20 pm) Seven of nine listed park areas/features are open, while Olympic Pipe and Big Air are closed. The road is chain-free, although chains must still be carried because of an active road hazard advisory. Four of six car parks are open, with Carpark B and Carpark C full. Ski touring access is open, while Mt Cardrona is on hold.",
